# Shared contracts (`@app/shared` → `packages/shared`)

One file per domain, re-exported from `src/index.ts`. Current modules: `app`, `brand`, `auth`, `account`,
`tenant`, `task`, `article`, `billing`, `admin`, `agent`. Both API and web import from `@app/shared` —
this package is the single source of truth for request/response shapes. Change a shape here and
whichever side you forgot stops compiling; that's the point.

`brand.ts` is product identity (`displayName`, `tagline`, `description`, `mcpServerName`,
`repoUrl`, `desktopArtifactBasename`, `defaultMailFrom`) — not a Zod contract. Day-1 rename
starts there; the web mark lives in `apps/web/src/brand/`; run `npm run sync:brand` for Tauri
shells and the macOS install script.

Resource domains (task, article, …) get their own `src/<domain>.ts`. Platform/support domains may
share a file when shapes are tightly coupled (e.g. auth session DTOs), but prefer a dedicated file
once a domain has its own API surface (`account.ts` for profile / password / API keys). `usage` is
API-only ledger code today — spend for the UI is on `TenantBillingDto` in `billing.ts`.
`OkDto` / `ApiErrorBody` live in `app.ts`; invite accept returns `AcceptInviteResultDto` in `tenant.ts`.

- Input validation: a descriptive Zod schema with real constraints (`trim`, `min`, `max`). Prefer
  `<thing>InputSchema` for resource create/update bodies (e.g. `taskInputSchema`, `articleInputSchema`); auth/account
  flows use intent names (`loginSchema`, `createApiKeySchema`). Multipart cover uploads validate in-route (article)
- Output: a plain `type XxxDto` with JSON-safe fields — dates are ISO **strings**, never `Date`; nullable fields are explicit (`string | null`)
- Zod is the only runtime dependency. No imports from apps, no DB or HTTP knowledge here
- New domain = new `src/<domain>.ts` + `export * from "./<domain>"` in `src/index.ts`
